1:make-docs setup skills
2:
3:Sync or remove managed make-docs skills without changing the docs scaffold.
4:Adopt existing first-party copies only after reviewing their files and ownership.
5:
6:Usage:
7:  make-docs setup skills [options]
8:
9:General options:
10:  --target <dir>                 Sync skills for a different make-docs install directory.
11:  --dry-run                      Show planned skill changes without writing files.
12:  --yes                          Skip interactive prompts.
13:  --help, -h                     Show help for this command.
14:
15:Platform options:
16:  --no-codex                     Skip Codex skill files.
17:  --no-claude-code               Skip Claude Code skill files.
18:  Deprecated aliases: --no-agents, --no-claude
19:
20:Skill options:
21:  --remove                       Remove managed skills owned by make-docs.
22:  --skill-manifest <file>       Use an explicit local skills manifest for this run.
23:  --skill-scope project|global   Choose whether skills install in the repo or the global Codex home.
24:  --selected-skills <csv|all|none>
25:                                  Replace the selected skill set.
26:  --adopt-existing <csv>          Review named, selected first-party copies for adoption.
27:  --review <digest>               Apply the exact reviewed adoption plan.
28:
29:Adoption dry runs write no files or Store records. Review shows backups,
30:file changes, ownership changes, and blockers. Non-interactive adoption requires
31:the matching --review digest; --yes alone is insufficient. Interactive adoption
32:shows the same plan before confirmation. Adoption cannot be combined with --remove.
33:
34:Examples:
35:  make-docs setup skills
36:  make-docs setup skills --dry-run
37:  make-docs setup skills --remove
38:  make-docs setup skills --skill-scope global
39:  make-docs setup skills --selected-skills all
40:  make-docs setup skills --selected-skills preflight --adopt-existing preflight --dry-run
41:  make-docs setup skills --selected-skills preflight --adopt-existing preflight --review <digest> --yes
